Refactor eye tracking pipeline and improve code organization
    Description:
        Changes:
        - Introduced reusable helper functions:
            - euclidean_distance()
            - landmark_to_pixel()
            - calculate_iris_center()
            - calculate_gaze()
        - Moved gaze and blink thresholds into global constants.
        - Refactored repeated landmark-to-pixel conversion using helper functions.
        - Centralized eye-specific configuration using the EYES dictionary.
        - Simplified iris center calculation.
        - Reduced duplicate code and improved readability.
        - Standardized gaze ratio, direction, and blink detection workflow.
        - Improved maintainability in preparation for continuous gaze estimation and calibration.


5-08-2026 21:17
    Implemented the first complete gaze estimation pipeline.

    Features added:
    - Refactored gaze calculation into reusable helper functions.
    - Added horizontal and vertical gaze ratio estimation.
    - Added iris center computation.
    - Added blink detection using Eye Aspect Ratio (EAR).
    - Added temporal smoothing for gaze measurements.
    - Added 2D gaze visualization using a movable indicator inside a bounding box.
    - Introduced horizontal and vertical normalization logic.
    - Added groundwork for gaze calibration by tracking calibration bounds.
    - Improved code readability with constants, helper functions, and structured eye configuration.

7-08-2026 23:08
    Implemented a calibration-based gaze tracking pipeline.

    Features added:
    - Added horizontal and vertical gaze ratio calculations.
    - Implemented moving-average smoothing for gaze estimation.
    - Added calibration workflow using keyboard inputs (L, R, U, D).
    - Stored calibration boundaries for left, right, up, and down gaze.
    - Normalized raw gaze ratios into a 0–1 coordinate system.
    - Added a visual gaze box with a cursor representing normalized gaze position.
    - Added calibration status indicators and reset functionality.
    - Added safeguards against invalid calibration values and division by zero.
    - Refactored the tracking loop for clearer separation of gaze estimation, smoothing, calibration, and visualization.

    Known limitations:
    - Vertical gaze estimation is still unstable due to eyelid movement and will be redesigned in the next iteration.